    "pages": [
      {
        "id": "p0",
        "title": "The Math of Red vs Blue",
        "showHud": "rf",
        "text": "Red RF builds in about 9 seconds; a full Blue gauge takes 35. Per second spent building, Red IC combos pay roughly TWICE the damage of Blue ones - in the time you save up one Blue, you could have spent Red three times."
      },
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "title": "Blue Is Powerful but Volatile",
        "showHud": "rf",
        "text": "Blue RF DRAINS when you get hit - and most characters have routes built to maximize that drain. Hoarding Blue makes you a target. Blue earns its keep when the threshold arrives naturally mid-combo, or spent on an invincible RF reversal that Red could never cancel."
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "title": "The Drill",
        "text": "Three ways to spend: the Red IC combo (stable, cheap, repeatable), the Blue IC route when the gauge is already there, and the defensive Blue IC that buys your way out of a blocked reversal. Spend on purpose - never by accident."
      }
    ],
